WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.543
Settlement tells you what a transaction moved.

2
00:00:03.543 --> 00:00:09.724
The Invoice check answers the question a business really has: did this transaction pay this invoice?

3
00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:17.555
You enter the receiving account, an optional destination tag, the asset and the amount you expect.

4
00:00:17.555 --> 00:00:19.744
Verified means it paid the invoice.

5
00:00:20.194 --> 00:00:25.293
Hold means a person should look first, for example when a payment is larger than the invoice.

6
00:00:25.743 --> 00:00:30.287
Rejected means it did not pay, and the reason is given in plain words.

7
00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:31.780
Only verified is green.

8
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.491
It credits only what was delivered, never the amount the payment states.

9
00:00:37.941 --> 00:00:41.887
It compares amounts exactly, digit by digit, and never rounds.

10
00:00:42.337 --> 00:00:51.212
And by default it reads the transaction from two independent node operators, X R P L Labs and Ripple, and says so if they disagree.

11
00:00:52.912 --> 00:00:55.152
Here is a real payment on mainnet.

12
00:00:55.152 --> 00:01:02.463
It asked for one hundred sixty-two point six nine nine C S C and delivered one hundred sixty-one point one six.

13
00:01:02.463 --> 00:01:07.931
Checked against the full amount, with partial payments not allowed, it is rejected.

14
00:01:08.381 --> 00:01:14.213
Checked against the amount actually delivered, with partial payments allowed, it is verified.

15
00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:18.791
The Academy's labs let you run both, and five more real cases on testnet.
